  contentMd: "# Consumer Health Data Privacy Policy\n\n**Effective date:** [EFFECTIVE DATE]\n\nThis policy explains how [COMPANY] (\"we\", \"us\") handles **consumer health\ndata** in [APP NAME], as required by the Washington My Health My Data Act\nand similar laws in Nevada and Connecticut. It applies in addition to our\n[Privacy Policy](./privacy-policy.md); for consumer health data, this policy\ncontrols.\n\n## Categories of consumer health data we collect\n\n- Workout and exercise data: sessions, exercises, sets, repetitions, loads,\n  perceived-effort ratings, and training programs.\n- Body measurements: bodyweight and other measurements you record.\n- Progress photos you choose to add.\n- Notes you attach to workouts or exercises (which may describe physical\n  condition, e.g., soreness or injury).\n- Messages you exchange with the AI coach, which may contain health\n  information you include.\n- Derived training metrics computed from the above (e.g., estimated training\n  maxes, volume totals, readiness suggestions).\n\nWe collect this data **only from you** — from what you enter into the app.\nWe do not collect consumer health data from other sources, and we do not use\ninferences to derive health data from non-health data.\n\n## Why we collect and use it\n\nWe collect and use consumer health data **solely to provide the services you\nask for**: recording your training, displaying your history and progress,\nderiving your program's targets, and generating coaching responses. We also\nuse it as necessary to secure the Service and comply with law.\n\nWe do **not** use consumer health data for advertising or marketing, and we\ndo **not** use it to train AI models.\n\n## How we get your consent\n\n- **Collection:** at signup, we ask for your consent to collect the health\n  data the Service needs to function.\n- **Sharing with our processors:** we separately ask for your consent before\n  any consumer health data is shared with the service providers below.\n- You may withdraw consent at any time in Settings or by contacting\n  [CONTACT EMAIL]. Because this data *is* the Service, withdrawing consent\n  for collection means closing your account; we will delete your data as\n  described below.\n\n## Who we share it with\n\nWe do not sell consumer health data, and we will not share it with third\nparties for their own purposes. It is processed only by service providers\nacting under contract on our behalf:\n\n| Processor | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| Supabase (database hosting) | Storing your training and body data |\n| Vercel (application hosting) | Serving the application |\n| [LLM PROVIDER] | Generating AI coach responses from your messages and training context |\n| Sentry (error monitoring) | Diagnostics if an error involves in-flight data |\n\nOur analytics provider (PostHog) is deliberately **not** a processor of\nconsumer health data: analytics events carry only counts, durations, and\ncoarse categories — never exercise names, loads, bodyweight, photos, or note\ntext.\n\nWe will disclose consumer health data if legally compelled (for example, by\na valid court order), and only to the extent required.\n\n## Your rights\n\nYou have the right to:\n\n- **Access** the consumer health data we hold about you (your data is also\n  visible and exportable in the app at any time);\n- **Withdraw consent** to our collection or sharing of your consumer health\n  data;\n- **Delete** your consumer health data. Deletion requests are honored for\n  the live database promptly and for backups on their ordinary aging\n  schedule; we also instruct our processors to delete.\n\nTo exercise any right, use the in-app Settings controls or email\n[CONTACT EMAIL]. We will respond within the time required by law. We will\nnot discriminate against you for exercising your rights. If we deny a\nrequest, you may appeal by replying to our response; if your appeal is\ndenied, you may contact the Washington Attorney General (or your state's\nattorney general).\n\n## Contact\n\n[COMPANY]\n[MAILING ADDRESS]\n[CONTACT EMAIL]\n",
